<div class="note warn">
    <span class="nh">Experimental feature — how to turn it on</span>
    Agent teams are an <strong>experimental feature</strong>. You turn them on with an environment variable in <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>:
    <pre><code>"env": {
  "CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS": "1"
}</code></pre>
    There is a bug where they come up as isolated subagents if dynamic loading fails, so if you do not see the agents, <code>/exit</code> and come back in, then check with <code>/agents</code>.
</div>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">Where do the files appear</span>
    The generated agent and skill definitions are left under the project's <code>.claude</code>, so you can <strong>share them with the team via Git</strong>. However, <strong>the plugin itself has to be installed on each machine separately</strong>. The history of configuration changes is recorded in <code>CLAUDE.md</code>. This continues into <a href="#!hnp-agents-skills">Agent · skill design</a>, which covers team design itself in more depth.
</div>
